Z||000000||MoneypitGT||11-09-2000||12:31 AM||||So how hard....or easy is the 4.9 swap. The motors are fairly cheap and bolt right up, so I'm told. Are nice headers made for it, and has anyone done one?? <BR>  Chris<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> '87 GT<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-09-2000||04:14 PM||||Chris, I'm working on a 4.9 swap, but it's in a custom chassis. The engine does bolt to a stock fiero trans, but for a manual, you need a custom made or re-drilled flywheel. The 4.9 uses cast iron exhaust manifolds, but I'm thinking about using the tube type manifolds from a 4.1 V8 for weight savings. As far as actual headers, they would have to be custom made. I bought a complete '91 Cadillac for $350 from a salvage yard. It has minor front end damage but runs and drives great. The 4.9 makes 200 hp and 275 ft/lb torque stock. Because it's aluminum, it weighs about the same as a 2.8. The swap requires very much of the same mods as a 3800 swap. The auto trans that comes with the 4.9 is also the same one that's used with the 3800. For more info, check <A HREF="http://www.azstarnet.com/~gduncan/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.azstarnet.com/~gduncan/index.html</A>  and <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/</A>  . I've only ever heard of a few 4.9 liter Fieros, and I've never seen one. I'm not sure why it's not more popular.<P>By the way, I live right up the road in Zionsville. Nice to see another member from PA. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||14
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||11-09-2000||06:49 PM||||If you use a Fiero trans, you have to grind a little for starter clearance. <P>I haven't found a motor yet so I haven't done the swap.||||reg||1
